IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Legislation Act 2019 (New Zealand) -- LAYER 1: PART 2, COMMENCEMENT ORDERS, AMENDMENT AND REPEAL (ss 29 to 38).
-- s 24 (outline of commencement provisions) is a guide only and carries no rule: see the coverage table in NOTES.md.
-- ss 25 to 28 (when legislation comes into force) and s 39 (time of repeal) are in nz-interpretation-time.l4, which decides days and moments.
-- Every rule below is a provision of Part 2, so section 9(1) (nz-part2-principles.l4) says first whether it applies to the legislation in question.

§ `Section 29 -- Power to make commencement order`

-- src:234 | includes a power to state a time of commencement on the date that is set; and
-- (a) includes a power to state a time of commencement on the date that is set. The power belongs to whoever may bring the legislation into force by Order in Council.
-- src:232 | 29 Power to make commencement order
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 29(1)(a) (src:232) (src:234)
GIVEN `the Order in Council is made under a power to bring legislation into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an Order in Council may state a time of commencement on the date that is set` `the Order in Council is made under a power to bring legislation into force` MEANS
    `the Order in Council is made under a power to bring legislation into force`

-- (b) is capable of being exercised more than once to amend, revoke, or replace an Order in Council made in a previous exercise of the power,
-- so long as each re-exercise takes effect before the commencement takes effect. The commencement takes effect at the start of its day unless a time is stated (s 27), so a
-- re-exercise on the same day as the commencement is not before it unless the order states a time and the re-exercise takes effect before that time (fork F8).
-- src:235 | is capable of being exercised more than once to amend, revoke, or replace an Order in Council made in a previous exercise of the power, so long as each re-exercise of the power takes effect before the commencement takes effect; and
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 29(1)(b) (src:235)
GIVEN `the day the re-exercise takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the day the commencement takes effect` IS A DATE
      `the order states a time on that day and the re-exercise takes effect before that time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a commencement order may be amended, revoked or replaced by a re-exercise of the power taking effect on` `the day the re-exercise takes effect` `when the commencement takes effect on` `the day the commencement takes effect` `and` `the order states a time on that day and the re-exercise takes effect before that time` MEANS
        (`the day the re-exercise takes effect` LESS THAN `the day the commencement takes effect`)
     OR (    (`the day the re-exercise takes effect` EQUALS `the day the commencement takes effect`)
         AND `the order states a time on that day and the re-exercise takes effect before that time`)

-- (c) includes a power to make 1 or more orders setting different dates for different provisions of the legislation.
-- src:236 | includes a power to make 1 or more orders setting different dates for different provisions of the legislation; and
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 29(1)(c) (src:236)
GIVEN `the number of orders` IS A NUMBER
      `the provisions are provisions of the legislation the power brings into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`orders may set different dates for different provisions` `the number of orders` `the provisions are provisions of the legislation the power brings into force` MEANS
        (`the number of orders` AT LEAST 1)
    AND `the provisions are provisions of the legislation the power brings into force`

DECLARE `Extent of a commencement` IS ONE OF
    `The whole provision comes into force`
    `The provision comes into force only for the stated purpose, and only the identified parts come into force`
    `Section 29(1)(d) gives no such power here: the text does not say what the order does`

-- (d) includes (if there is a provision where its commencement would otherwise operate to give effect to other parts of legislation) a power to commence
-- the provision only for the purpose of giving effect to some, but not other, parts of that legislation. (2) If that power is exercised, the provision
-- comes into force only for that purpose and only the identified parts come into force.
-- src:240 | If the power referred to in subsection (1)﻿(d) is exercised, the provision comes into force only for that purpose and only the identified parts come into force.
-- src:237 | includes (if there is a provision where its commencement would otherwise operate to give effect to other parts of legislation) a power to commence the provision only for the purpose of giving effect to some, but not other, parts of that legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 29(1)(d) and (2) (src:237) (src:240)
GIVEN `the provision's commencement would otherwise operate to give effect to other parts of legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the order commences the provision only for the purpose of giving effect to some, but not other, parts of that legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Extent of a commencement`
`what comes into force when an order commences a provision` `the provision's commencement would otherwise operate to give effect to other parts of legislation` `the order commences the provision only for the purpose of giving effect to some, but not other, parts of that legislation` MEANS
    IF `the order commences the provision only for the purpose of giving effect to some, but not other, parts of that legislation`
    THEN IF `the provision's commencement would otherwise operate to give effect to other parts of legislation`
         THEN `The provision comes into force only for the stated purpose, and only the identified parts come into force`
         ELSE `Section 29(1)(d) gives no such power here: the text does not say what the order does`
    ELSE `The whole provision comes into force`

§ `Section 30 -- Amendments part of, and construed with, legislation amended`

-- src:243 | Amending legislation is part of the legislation that it amends.
-- src:242 | 30 Amendments part of, and construed with, legislation amended
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 30(1) (src:242) (src:243)
GIVEN `the legislation is amended by the amending legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`amending legislation is part of the legislation that it amends` `the legislation is amended by the amending legislation` MEANS
    `the legislation is amended by the amending legislation`

-- src:244 | Amending legislation must be construed with the legislation that it amends.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 30(2) (src:244)
GIVEN `the legislation is amended by the amending legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`amending legislation must be construed with the legislation that it amends` `the legislation is amended by the amending legislation` MEANS
    `the legislation is amended by the amending legislation`

§ `Section 31 -- References to repeal or amendment extend to other ceasing of effect`

-- The printed items are members, and so is each thing an item names (ruling C): an implied repeal, an implied amendment; a disapplication to a person, to a subject matter, to a circumstance.
DECLARE `Kind of change to legislation` IS ONE OF
    `an express repeal`
    `an express amendment`
    `an implied repeal or amendment`
    `an implied repeal`
    `an implied amendment`
    `a change that removes or limits the effect of the legislation`
    `a change that removes the effect of the legislation`
    `a change that limits the effect of the legislation`
    `a change that disapplies the legislation to a person, subject matter or circumstance`
    `a change that disapplies the legislation to a person`
    `a change that disapplies the legislation to a subject matter`
    `a change that disapplies the legislation to a circumstance`
    `a change of another kind`

-- src:245 | 31 References to repeal or amendment extend to other ceasing of effect
-- src:246 | A reference in sections 32 to 36, 38, and 39 to repealing or amending legislation includes a reference to—
-- src:247 | an implied repeal or amendment; and
-- src:248 | a change that removes or limits the effect of the legislation; and
-- src:249 | a change that disapplies the legislation to any person, subject matter, or circumstance.
-- "A reference in sections 32 to 36, 38, and 39 to repealing or amending legislation includes (a) an implied repeal or amendment; (b) a change that removes or
-- limits the effect of the legislation; (c) a change that disapplies the legislation to any person, subject matter, or circumstance."
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 31 (src:245-249)
GIVEN section IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 31 reaches section` section MEANS
        ((section AT LEAST 32) AND (section AT MOST 36))
     OR (section EQUALS 38)
     OR (section EQUALS 39)

@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 31 (src:246-249)
GIVEN section IS A NUMBER
      change IS A `Kind of change to legislation`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a change counts as repealing or amending legislation in section` section `when the change is` change MEANS
    IF `section 31 reaches section` section
    THEN CONSIDER change
         WHEN `an express repeal` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `an express amendment` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `an implied repeal or amendment` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `an implied repeal` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `an implied amendment` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a change that removes or limits the effect of the legislation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a change that removes the effect of the legislation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a change that limits the effect of the legislation` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a change that disapplies the legislation to a person, subject matter or circumstance` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a change that disapplies the legislation to a person` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a change that disapplies the legislation to a subject matter` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a change that disapplies the legislation to a circumstance` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `a change of another kind` THEN NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 32 -- Effect of repeal or amendment generally`

-- The printed items of s 32(1) are members, and so is each thing they name (ruling C).
DECLARE `Effect of a repeal or amendment` IS ONE OF
    `affects the validity, invalidity, effect or consequences of anything done or suffered`
    `affects the validity of anything done or suffered`
    `affects the invalidity of anything done or suffered`
    `affects the effect of anything done or suffered`
    `affects the consequences of anything done or suffered`
    `affects an existing right, interest, title, immunity, duty, status or capacity`
    `affects an existing right`
    `affects an existing interest`
    `affects an existing title`
    `affects an existing immunity`
    `affects an existing duty`
    `affects an existing status`
    `affects an existing capacity`
    `affects an amendment made by the legislation to other legislation`
    `affects the previous operation of the legislation or anything done or suffered under it`
    `affects the previous operation of the legislation`
    `affects anything done or suffered under the legislation`
    `revives a thing that is not in force or existing when the repeal or amendment takes effect`
    `revives a thing that is not in force when the repeal or amendment takes effect`
    `revives a thing that is not existing when the repeal or amendment takes effect`
    `revives legislation that has been repealed`
    `revives a rule of law that has been abolished`
    `has another effect`

-- src:250 | 32 Effect of repeal or amendment generally
-- src:251 | The repeal or amendment of legislation does not—
-- src:252 | affect the validity, invalidity, effect, or consequences of anything done or suffered:
-- src:253 | affect an existing right, interest, title, immunity, duty, status, or capacity:
-- src:254 | affect an amendment made by the legislation to other legislation:
-- src:255 | affect the previous operation of the legislation or anything done or suffered under it:
-- src:256 | revive any thing that is not in force or existing at the time the repeal or amendment takes effect.
-- src:257 | The repeal of legislation does not revive—
-- src:258 | legislation that has been repealed; or
-- src:259 | a rule of law that has been abolished.
-- (1) The repeal or amendment of legislation does not (a) affect the validity ... of anything done or suffered; (b) affect an existing right ...; (c) affect an amendment
-- made by the legislation to other legislation; (d) affect the previous operation of the legislation ...; (e) revive any thing that is not in force or existing at the time the repeal or amendment
-- takes effect. (2) The repeal of legislation does not revive (a) legislation that has been repealed; or (b) a rule of law that has been abolished.
-- Subsection (2) is about repeal alone; for an amendment, reviving repealed legislation or an abolished rule would be reviving a thing "not in force or existing", which (1)(e) already forbids.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 32 (src:250-259)
GIVEN effect IS AN `Effect of a repeal or amendment`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`a repeal or amendment of legislation does this, under section 32` effect MEANS
    CONSIDER effect
    WHEN `affects the validity, invalidity, effect or consequences of anything done or suffered` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `affects the validity of anything done or suffered` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `affects the invalidity of anything done or suffered` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `affects the effect of anything done or suffered` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `affects the consequences of anything done or suffered` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `affects an existing right, interest, title, immunity, duty, status or capacity` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `affects an existing right` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `affects an existing interest` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `affects an existing title` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `affects an existing immunity` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `affects an existing duty` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `affects an existing status` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `affects an existing capacity` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `affects an amendment made by the legislation to other legislation` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `affects the previous operation of the legislation or anything done or suffered under it` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `affects the previous operation of the legislation` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `affects anything done or suffered under the legislation` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `revives a thing that is not in force or existing when the repeal or amendment takes effect` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `revives a thing that is not in force when the repeal or amendment takes effect` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `revives a thing that is not existing when the repeal or amendment takes effect` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `revives legislation that has been repealed` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `revives a rule of law that has been abolished` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `has another effect` THEN NOTHING

§ `Section 33 -- Effect of repeal or amendment on existing rights and proceedings`

-- src:262 | the completion of a matter or thing that relates to an existing right, interest, title, immunity, duty, status, or capacity (a legal position); or
-- (1) The repeal or amendment of legislation does not affect (a) the completion of a matter or thing that relates to an existing right, interest, title, immunity, duty,
-- status, or capacity (a legal position); or (b) the commencing of a proceeding that relates to an existing legal position; or (c) the completion of a proceeding commenced
-- or in progress under the legislation.
-- src:260 | 33 Effect of repeal or amendment on existing rights and proceedings
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 33(1)(a) (src:260) (src:262)
GIVEN `the matter or thing relates to an existing legal position` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the completion of the matter or thing is unaffected by the repeal or amendment` `the matter or thing relates to an existing legal position` MEANS
    `the matter or thing relates to an existing legal position`

-- src:263 | the commencing of a proceeding that relates to an existing legal position; or
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 33(1)(b) (src:263)
GIVEN `the proceeding relates to an existing legal position` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the commencing of the proceeding is unaffected by the repeal or amendment` `the proceeding relates to an existing legal position` MEANS
    `the proceeding relates to an existing legal position`

-- src:264 | the completion of a proceeding commenced or in progress under the legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 33(1)(c) (src:264)
GIVEN `the proceeding was commenced or in progress under the legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the completion of the proceeding is unaffected by the repeal or amendment` `the proceeding was commenced or in progress under the legislation` MEANS
    `the proceeding was commenced or in progress under the legislation`

-- (2) Repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect for the purposes stated in subsection (1) as if the legislation had not been repealed or amended.
-- src:265 | Repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect for the purposes stated in subsection (1) as if the legislation had not been repealed or amended.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 33(2) (src:265)
GIVEN `a matter or thing is protected by section 33(1)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a proceeding is protected by section 33(1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a proceeding is protected by section 33(1)(c)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect for the purposes of section 33(1)` `a matter or thing is protected by section 33(1)(a)` `a proceeding is protected by section 33(1)(b)` `a proceeding is protected by section 33(1)(c)` MEANS
    `a matter or thing is protected by section 33(1)(a)` OR `a proceeding is protected by section 33(1)(b)` OR `a proceeding is protected by section 33(1)(c)`

§ `Section 34 -- Effect of repeal or amendment on prior offences and breaches of legislation`

-- src:267 | The repeal or amendment of legislation does not affect a liability to a penalty or any other remedy or relief, or to an order or a direction, for an offence or for a breach of any legislation committed before the repeal or amendment.
-- (1) The repeal or amendment of legislation does not affect a liability to a penalty or any other remedy or relief, or to an order or a direction, for an offence or for a breach of
-- any legislation committed before the repeal or amendment. "Before": the repeal or amendment takes effect at the start of its day (s 39 for a repeal; s 27 for commencement),
-- so an offence committed on that day is not before it (fork F9).
-- src:266 | 34 Effect of repeal or amendment on prior offences and breaches of legislation
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 34(1) (src:266) (src:267)
GIVEN `the day the offence or breach was committed` IS A DATE
      `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the liability for an offence or breach committed on` `the day the offence or breach was committed` `is unaffected by a repeal or amendment taking effect on` `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect` MEANS
    `the day the offence or breach was committed` LESS THAN `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect`

-- The printed items of s 34(2) are members, and so is each thing they name (ruling C).
DECLARE `Purpose for which repealed legislation continues` IS ONE OF
    `investigating the offence or breach`
    `commencing or completing a proceeding for the offence or breach`
    `commencing a proceeding for the offence or breach`
    `completing a proceeding for the offence or breach`
    `imposing a penalty, or any other remedy or relief, or making or giving an order or a direction, for the offence or breach`
    `imposing a penalty for the offence or breach`
    `imposing any other remedy or relief for the offence or breach`
    `making an order for the offence or breach`
    `giving an order for the offence or breach`
    `making a direction for the offence or breach`
    `giving a direction for the offence or breach`
    `another purpose`

-- (2) Repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if it had not been repealed or amended for the purpose of (a) investigating; (b) commencing or completing a proceeding;
-- (c) imposing a penalty or other remedy or relief, or making or giving an order or direction, for the offence or breach.
-- src:268 | Repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if it had not been repealed or amended for the purpose of—
-- src:271 | imposing a penalty, or any other remedy or relief, or making or giving an order or a direction, for the offence or breach.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 34(2) (src:268-271)
GIVEN purpose IS A `Purpose for which repealed legislation continues`
      `the day the offence or breach was committed` IS A DATE
      `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`repealed or amended legislation continues to have effect as if not repealed or amended for the purpose of` purpose `for an offence or breach committed on` `the day the offence or breach was committed` `before a repeal or amendment taking effect on` `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect` MEANS
    CONSIDER purpose
    WHEN `investigating the offence or breach` THEN JUST (`the day the offence or breach was committed` LESS THAN `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect`)
    WHEN `commencing or completing a proceeding for the offence or breach` THEN JUST (`the day the offence or breach was committed` LESS THAN `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect`)
    WHEN `commencing a proceeding for the offence or breach` THEN JUST (`the day the offence or breach was committed` LESS THAN `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect`)
    WHEN `completing a proceeding for the offence or breach` THEN JUST (`the day the offence or breach was committed` LESS THAN `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect`)
    WHEN `imposing a penalty, or any other remedy or relief, or making or giving an order or a direction, for the offence or breach` THEN JUST (`the day the offence or breach was committed` LESS THAN `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect`)
    WHEN `imposing a penalty for the offence or breach` THEN JUST (`the day the offence or breach was committed` LESS THAN `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect`)
    WHEN `imposing any other remedy or relief for the offence or breach` THEN JUST (`the day the offence or breach was committed` LESS THAN `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect`)
    WHEN `making an order for the offence or breach` THEN JUST (`the day the offence or breach was committed` LESS THAN `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect`)
    WHEN `giving an order for the offence or breach` THEN JUST (`the day the offence or breach was committed` LESS THAN `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect`)
    WHEN `making a direction for the offence or breach` THEN JUST (`the day the offence or breach was committed` LESS THAN `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect`)
    WHEN `giving a direction for the offence or breach` THEN JUST (`the day the offence or breach was committed` LESS THAN `the day the repeal or amendment takes effect`)
    -- Ruling B (fork F11): s 34(2) is a closed list of three purposes, so another purpose is not given by this subsection (JUST FALSE); section 33(2), 35 and 36 give their own continuations.
    WHEN `another purpose` THEN JUST FALSE

§ `Section 35 -- Powers exercised under repealed or amended legislation have continuing effect`

-- src:272 | 35 Powers exercised under repealed or amended legislation have continuing effect
-- src:273 | Anything done in the exercise of a power under repealed or amended legislation, and that is in effect immediately before that repeal or amendment, continues to have effect as if it had been exercised under any other legislation—
-- src:274 | that, with or without modification, replaces, or that corresponds to, the legislation repealed or amended; and
-- src:275 | under which the power could be exercised.
-- Anything done in the exercise of a power under repealed or amended legislation, and that is in effect immediately before that repeal or amendment, continues to have effect as if it
-- had been exercised under any other legislation (a) that, with or without modification, replaces, or that corresponds to, the legislation repealed or amended; and (b) under which the power could be exercised.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 35 (src:272) (src:273-275)
GIVEN `it was done in the exercise of a power under the repealed or amended legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in effect immediately before the repeal or amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other legislation replaces, or corresponds to, the legislation repealed or amended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power could be exercised under the other legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a thing done in the exercise of a power continues to have effect as if exercised under the other legislation` `it was done in the exercise of a power under the repealed or amended legislation` `it is in effect immediately before the repeal or amendment` `the other legislation replaces, or corresponds to, the legislation repealed or amended` `the power could be exercised under the other legislation` MEANS
        `it was done in the exercise of a power under the repealed or amended legislation`
    AND `it is in effect immediately before the repeal or amendment`
    AND `the other legislation replaces, or corresponds to, the legislation repealed or amended`
    AND `the power could be exercised under the other legislation`

§ `Section 36 -- Legislation made under repealed legislation has continuing effect`

-- src:277 | Any legislation made under repealed legislation, and that is in force immediately before that repeal, continues in force as if it had been made under any other legislation—
-- src:278 | that, with or without modification, replaces, or that corresponds to, the legislation repealed; and
-- src:279 | under which it could be made.
-- (1) Any legislation made under repealed legislation, and that is in force immediately before that repeal, continues in force as if it had been made under any other legislation (a) that,
-- with or without modification, replaces, or that corresponds to, the legislation repealed; and (b) under which it could be made.
-- src:276 | 36 Legislation made under repealed legislation has continuing effect
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 36(1) (src:276) (src:277-279)
GIVEN `it was made under the repealed legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in force immediately before the repeal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other legislation replaces, or corresponds to, the legislation repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it could be made under the other legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`legislation made under repealed legislation continues in force as if made under the other legislation` `it was made under the repealed legislation` `it is in force immediately before the repeal` `the other legislation replaces, or corresponds to, the legislation repealed` `it could be made under the other legislation` MEANS
        `it was made under the repealed legislation`
    AND `it is in force immediately before the repeal`
    AND `the other legislation replaces, or corresponds to, the legislation repealed`
    AND `it could be made under the other legislation`

-- (2) Legislation that continues in force may be amended or revoked as if it had been made under the legislation that replaces, or that corresponds to, the repealed legislation.
-- src:280 | Legislation that continues in force may be amended or revoked as if it had been made under the legislation that replaces, or that corresponds to, the repealed legislation.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 36(2) (src:280)
GIVEN `it continues in force under section 36(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`legislation may be amended or revoked as if made under the replacing legislation` `it continues in force under section 36(1)` MEANS
    `it continues in force under section 36(1)`

§ `Section 37 -- How to apply references to new legislation that is not yet in force`

DECLARE `What a reference to new legislation is a reference to` IS ONE OF
    `The whole or the corresponding part of the existing legislation`

-- src:281 | 37 How to apply references to new legislation that is not yet in force
-- src:282 | This section applies if legislation (new legislation)—
-- src:283 | is to replace (with or without modification), or is to correspond to, existing legislation; and
-- src:284 | is not yet in force.
-- src:285 | A reference in legislation to the new legislation is, until that new legislation comes into force, a reference to the whole or the corresponding part of the existing legislation.
-- This section applies if legislation (new legislation) is to replace (with or without modification), or is to correspond to, existing legislation; and is not yet in force.
-- A reference in legislation to the new legislation is, until that new legislation comes into force, a reference to the whole or the corresponding part of the existing legislation.
-- The new legislation is in force from the start of the day it comes into force (s 27, day level). If the section does not apply, the text does not say what the reference is to.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 37 (src:281) (src:282-285)
GIVEN `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `the new legislation is to replace, or is to correspond to, existing legislation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the new legislation comes into force` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE `What a reference to new legislation is a reference to`
`what a reference to new legislation is a reference to on` `the day asked about` `when the new legislation replaces or corresponds to existing legislation` `the new legislation is to replace, or is to correspond to, existing legislation` `and comes into force` `the day the new legislation comes into force` MEANS
    IF `the new legislation is to replace, or is to correspond to, existing legislation`
    THEN CONSIDER `the day the new legislation comes into force`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST `The whole or the corresponding part of the existing legislation`
         WHEN JUST commencement THEN
             IF `the day asked about` LESS THAN commencement
             THEN JUST `The whole or the corresponding part of the existing legislation`
             ELSE NOTHING
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 38 -- How to apply references to repealed legislation`

DECLARE `What happens on repeal to a reference to the repealed legislation` IS ONE OF
    `The reference is a reference to the legislation that replaces, or corresponds to, the legislation repealed`
    `The legislation that refers to the repealed legislation is unaffected by the repeal`

-- src:286 | 38 How to apply references to repealed legislation
-- src:287 | The repeal of legislation does not affect legislation in which the repealed legislation is applied, incorporated, or referred to.
-- src:288 | A reference in legislation to repealed legislation is a reference to legislation that, with or without modification, replaces, or that corresponds to, the legislation repealed.
-- src:289 | Subsection (1) is subject to subsection (2).
-- (1) The repeal of legislation does not affect legislation in which the repealed legislation is applied, incorporated, or referred to.
-- (2) A reference in legislation to repealed legislation is a reference to legislation that, with or without modification, replaces, or that corresponds to, the legislation repealed.
-- (3) Subsection (1) is subject to subsection (2): where there is replacing or corresponding legislation, the reference is read as a reference to it; otherwise subsection (1) leaves the referring legislation as it is.
@ref Legislation Act 2019 s 38 (src:286) (src:287-289)
GIVEN `there is legislation that, with or without modification, replaces or corresponds to the legislation repealed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What happens on repeal to a reference to the repealed legislation`
`what a reference in legislation to repealed legislation is` `there is legislation that, with or without modification, replaces or corresponds to the legislation repealed` MEANS
    IF `there is legislation that, with or without modification, replaces or corresponds to the legislation repealed`
    THEN `The reference is a reference to the legislation that replaces, or corresponds to, the legislation repealed`
    ELSE `The legislation that refers to the repealed legislation is unaffected by the repeal`
